A. Commit message:
btrfs: check folio mapping after unlock in relocate_one_folio()

B. Change summary:
This patch ensures that the folio's mapping is checked after unlocking the folio to prevent a race condition where another thread might modify or remove the mapping, leading to a potential crash. If the mapping is not as expected, the operation retries.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/fs/btrfs/relocation.c b/fs/btrfs/relocation.c
index bf267bdfa8f81..db8b42f674b7c 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/relocation.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/relocation.c
@@ -2902,6 +2902,7 @@ static int relocate_one_folio(struct reloc_control *rc,
 	const bool use_rst = btrfs_need_stripe_tree_update(fs_info, rc->block_group->flags);
 
 	ASSERT(index <= last_index);
+again:
 	folio = filemap_lock_folio(inode->i_mapping, index);
 	if (IS_ERR(folio)) {
 
@@ -2937,6 +2938,11 @@ static int relocate_one_folio(struct reloc_control *rc,
 			ret = -EIO;
 			goto release_folio;
 		}
+		if (folio->mapping != inode->i_mapping) {
+			folio_unlock(folio);
+			folio_put(folio);
+			goto again;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/*
```